# The wire tile for a routing column three blocks wide: the north-south arm runs
# down the middle column (x = 1), the west-east arm along the middle row
# (z = 2). A repeater goes in the arm the signal enters by, as in the wire
# tile; entering from the west or east, that arm is the centre itself, so only
# a straight carries one.
tile wire_n
size 3 4 5
port W io 0 1 2
port E io 2 1 2
port N io 1 1 0
port S io 1 1 4

legend
  C minecraft:glass
  c minecraft:redstone_wire
  W minecraft:glass if W
  w minecraft:redstone_wire if W
  E minecraft:glass if E
  e minecraft:redstone_wire if E
  N minecraft:glass if N
  n minecraft:redstone_wire if N
  S minecraft:glass if S
  s minecraft:redstone_wire if S

layer 0
  .N.
  .N.
  WCE
  .S.
  .S.
layer 1
  .n.
  .n.
  wce
  .s.
  .s.
